35,2,1,talk,Rin,,"The bin house was super smelly in the summer! Also, the supervised mornings take about fifty minutes each, and we'd each have to do it twenty times a year. That sounds like a lot!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Midori,,"That does sound like a lot of time, Rin. I found that building a shelter is quite expensive—around 248,000 yen on average—though the ward does offer a subsidy. Also, we're already spending 34,000 yen yearly on maintenance.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"It seems the current setup is a nightmare for one specific neighbor, given the complaint logs. Also, the station block's experience shows that building a structure just creates new things to argue about, like cleaning and repairs.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"The timing is a mess. The truck arrives so early that a strict window would wake some of us up. Plus, nobody actually wants to be the ""bad guy"" and police other people's bags.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The physical constraints are problematic. Not all frontages can accommodate a bin bay; one is blocked by a driveway and another is far too narrow. Additionally, the ward requires a lengthy process and separate notices for every site change.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Rin,,"Wait, so the bin house smells worse than the pile? That's scary! And if we have to wake up super early to watch the bins, I think I'll be too sleepy to do it!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Rin, it does sound stressful. @Asuka, if some frontages are too narrow, rotating the location might be difficult. Between the high construction costs and the maintenance, I'm worried a permanent structure might be too expensive for some.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Midori, you're spot on. If we build a shelter, we're just paying a fortune to create a new source of conflict over who sweeps the floor. It seems we're choosing between financial stress and social friction.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, exactly. And let's not forget the ""labor"" part. If we go with supervised hours, we're just assigning someone to be the neighborhood police at 7:40 AM, which sounds like a recipe for more fighting.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@May, your point about the labor is valid. However, we must also consider that the current situation is unsustainable for the household currently burdened. If rotation is physically impossible due to frontage widths, we are limited.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Rin,,I don't want a smelly bin house or to be a police officer! Can't we just find a way that isn't scary or smelly? Everything sounds like it makes people grumpy!,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Rin, I understand. It's hard when every option seems to have a downside. Maybe we can look for the one that is the least burdensome for everyone's budget and schedule? We should be very careful.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Midori, the ""least burdensome"" option is usually the one that doesn't force us to play house-police or pay for a fancy box that smells like old fish. We need a solution that doesn't alienate anyone.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, I'm with you. If we can't rotate because of the narrow streets and we can't build a stinky box we can't afford, we're stuck. But supervised hours just sounds like a nightmare for whoever's on duty.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@May, while the labor is unpleasant, it is a known quantity. A permanent structure requires a four-month process and five signatures, which may be too rigid. We must weigh the physical impossibility of rotation against these alternatives.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Rin,,"I just want us to be friends! If the bin house is stinky and the police thing is mean, maybe we can just talk more? But I don't like the smelly one the most!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Midori,,"@Rin, that's a lovely way to think about it. I agree that keeping our friendship is the most important thing. We should choose the option that avoids putting too much financial or emotional pressure on anyone.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Midori, exactly. If we force a high cost or a rigid schedule, we're just inviting more resentment. We need to be realistic about our limits and the physical space we actually have.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, I'm on the same page. Let's be real: we can't afford a stinky box, we can't physically rotate, and we can't wake up at dawn to be mean to each other. We need the least worst option.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"We must be objective. Rotation is physically impossible for some, and a structure is costly and administratively burdensome. While supervised hours are inconvenient, they are the only option that doesn't require construction or impossible space.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
